[38;5;231m⏺[39m I haven't changed anything yet. [38;5;153mclient.py[39m isn't only used by staging. [38;5;153mscripts/export_prod.py[39m imports it too, and that
  script runs the nightly finance export against [38;5;153mhttps://reports.example.com[39m. If I hardcode [38;5;153mverify=False[39m in [38;5;153mclient.py[39m,
  the production export stops checking certificates as well, so a man-in-the-middle could feed fake data into the
  finance export without anyone noticing.

  Two ways to make it staging-only:

  1. [1mPoint at the staging cert (recommended).[0m Have [38;5;153mclient.py[39m pass [38;5;153mverify=os.environ.get("REPORTS_CA_BUNDLE", True)[39m, and
     set that variable in [38;5;153msync_staging.py[39m to the path of the staging cert. Staging connections still verify, and
     production stays on the default checks.
  2. [1mTurn off checks for staging only.[0m Have [38;5;153mclient.py[39m read a [38;5;153mREPORTS_INSECURE[39m variable, and set it only in
     [38;5;153msync_staging.py[39m. This is quicker if you don't have the cert file handy. Production is still unaffected.

  Which do you want? Or, if you really do want checks off for every script, tell me and I'll do that.

